<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>British comedian Russell Brand found guilty of rape, sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5aaadf07fd4ff060276b6b9de633a605cc967b35d314f0734b342e54edda6174</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:26:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261105-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-sexual-assault" /><summary type="html">A London jury on Thursday convicted British comedian and actor Russell Brand of one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France faces new protests as government seeks to prevent violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67a510884da6fbbb8e03719f7bf2b5169146f1a86a5be7e416a74aaa045d5ae8</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:19:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-faces-new-protests-as-government-seeks-to-prevent-violence" /><summary type="html">France faces new protests as the government seeks to prevent a repeat of October unrest. Protesters demand better public services, including education, and also critique the rising cost-of-living. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>French bank hit by cyberattack, hackers steal $100 million</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:243edab8e730dae8a94a5aa51eae146c88aadb4141831cca54b302e520438ca3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:09:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cyberattack-french-bank-says-online-hacking-stole-around-100-million" /><summary type="html">French regional bank Crédit Mutuel Arkéa said Wednesday it had been hit by a cyberattack that led to fraudulent transfers worth around 100 million euros ($112 million). The bank said the attack, which has since been "contained", allowed hackers to access its own accounts and transfer funds to other banks. Customer accounts were not affected, and no losses were reported by clients.</summary></entry><entry><title>Multiple flights in Europe diverted because of bomb threats after earlier hoaxes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4cf893096d59c477f9713d4309881008724ae04c9b67fc9a766dcb547f59068</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-multiple-flights-in-europe-diverted-because-of-bomb-threats-after-earlier-hoaxes" /><summary type="html">Multiple flights in Europe made emergency landings on Thursday after being diverted because of bomb threats. The incidents followed hoax bomb threats earlier this week that prompted searches, diversions and in one case a military escort.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dublin-Rome plane diverted to French base as 20 European flights hit by bomb hoaxes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fb767304671a7a3306105798c06f35b81c5787b2a2c8e28e626643a23f0d2f7</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:08:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261105-dublin-rome-flight-diverted-to-france-over-bomb-threat" /><summary type="html">An Airbus A320 ​flying from Dublin to Rome was safely diverted to France's Evreux airbase ​following a ‌bomb threat, ⁠the French prime minister's office said Thursday, in the latest in a series ‌of threats targeting flights across Europe. About 20 flights were hit by hoax bomb alerts across Europe, authorities said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>European leaders welcome Democrats' US midterms election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2540632bafdd56a12a3b9ce5b612905d8606f7fcec6e1a4e6fcd5e585c2988c</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:00:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win--9eb298186d7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win" /><summary type="html">European leaders voiced hopes for a reset with the United States on Wednesday, November 4, after voters delivered a huge midterm election defeat to President Donald Trump and his Republican party. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian's 'not expecting drastic change in US policy' after midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af3aaf5348b9359921775a0fc663104b3a610d93da6b95737e3943a71d9f070b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:26:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-s-not-expecting-drastic-change-in-us-policy-after-midterms--6a22a8195d02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-s-not-expecting-drastic-change-in-us-policy-after-midterms" /><summary type="html">Ukrainians do not expect the Democrats' victory in the US midterm elections is change much in regards to US policy on the war with Russia, or at least not quickly, says France 24's correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky has not reacted yet to the "blue wave" taking control of Congress in the US.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian households face increasing financial strain as war in Ukraine drags on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d82e0fa4fef45e87c5d924fa85f05d929eda96571b298347ecfbbadabed86161</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:05:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-russian-households-face-increasing-financial-strain-as-war-in-ukraine-drags-on--4000ebd21c3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-russian-households-face-increasing-financial-strain-as-war-in-ukraine-drags-on" /><summary type="html">As Moscow continues to launch strikes across Ukraine, Russian citizens are facing increasing financial strain. Since the start of the war in 2022, utility bills in Russia have risen by more than 50% – over 13% this year alone. These rising costs come as the country grapples with ongoing drone attacks originating from Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia are taking the war underground as drones saturate the battlefield</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e56ff3d1245ca13d0a42330c5f3c2f5470dc0ff6176c6c86947062fe2d7eccd2</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:52:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-ukraine-and-russia-are-taking-the-war-underground-as-drones-saturate-the-battlefield--10719a9e898a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-ukraine-and-russia-are-taking-the-war-underground-as-drones-saturate-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky last week heralded the success of Operation Veles, during which Kyiv sent troops deep into a disused gas pipeline in the Kupiansk region to confront Russian troops. These underground tactics, which Russian forces have been using for more than two years to slip past Ukrainian lines, are giving Kyiv a new strategy on the battlefield.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Bomb threats against European airlines force Warsaw airport closure, affect several flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2b90aaaa2c9e7620cfcf194e269987c5d90d6e3ed1871328eabb23dfa96a97b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:41:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-bomb-threats-disrupt-europe-flights--fca54047fb7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-bomb-threats-disrupt-europe-flights" /><summary type="html">Bomb threats targeted at least 10 European airlines on Tuesday, forcing the temporary closure of a Warsaw airport and affecting at least four Ryanair flights. No explosives were found after the planes all took off and landed safely in different European cities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles says he has greater understanding of 'horrors' of slavery, falls short of apology</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9aa2f5155a307728089fb524e06d8dabc6a57c6dd1b46857e3eba95610abd23</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:26:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology--ae418e66f435.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology" /><summary type="html">King Charles III told the heads of 56 Commonwealth countries on Tuesday that he has a greater understanding of the horrors of slavery, calling it a "shameful chapter of history". This comes as Prime Minister Andy Burnham said he was open to the United Kingdom apologising for the transatlantic slave trade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Poland foils attempted 'provocation' on Russian border, PM Tusk says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e02fe3134c764db5857cfcdece0f4b9a3ee3d59f9b7c6441025ea5b7456488b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:39:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-poland-prevented-attempted-provocation-russian-border-pm-tusk-says--aab9903dd48c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-poland-prevented-attempted-provocation-russian-border-pm-tusk-says" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Donald Tusk said Tuesday that Poland prevented an attempted "provocation" on its border with the Russian exclave of Kaliningrad overnight. He gave few details but said Polish security forces prevented any incident from happening.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French schools blockade resume on smaller scale as holidays end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91ee18b837b0b90e12e256137984e6b5d47b1d0fd2134b1135dc57fa66f1fd20</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:01:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-french-schools-blockade-resume-on-smaller-scale-as-holidays-end--e0c3a170632d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-french-schools-blockade-resume-on-smaller-scale-as-holidays-end" /><summary type="html">Students blockaded dozens of high schools across France on Tuesday to maintain pressure on the government over education reforms as trade unions prepared for a nationwide strike later this week. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cheese theft becomes rife among Europe's gangsters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60f2308bb9ad07b41b246d4434c977906201a664df555016a10525de7112f831</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T10:53:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261103-cheese-theft-becomes-rife-among-europe-s-gangsters--0e5372666128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261103-cheese-theft-becomes-rife-among-europe-s-gangsters" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, November 3: We look at reactions and analyses in Poland, where pro-European Prime Minister Donald Tusk is involved in a standoff with the nationalist president over the composition of the constitutional court. In other news, there's fresh outrage at big tech, after Google went rogue in Finland and cut down 250,000 trees for data centre projects. Finally, cheese is France's most stolen food product, and it's the stuff of cold, calculated crime.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>European force to hold first Ukraine support exercise in Poland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:184196029fc210e651b89fc405a9b11f7b5424bcefc50226d0d926bb41b2f3a1</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T01:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-european-force-to-hold-first-ukraine-support-exercise-in-poland--f3232a2d9c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-european-force-to-hold-first-ukraine-support-exercise-in-poland" /><summary type="html">Around 2,800 troops from 10 European countries will take part in a military exercise in southeastern Poland from November 9 to 22, testing a multinational force designed to support Ukraine after a potential ceasefire. Led by France and Britain, the force aims to bolster Ukraine's security without taking on an offensive role.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe's Gen Z protesters unite over living costs, housing and employment uncertainty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec014e2ab5b3c095faefd17468860cf5e184f1d4c04941b78c17c2c469c6412a</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T01:21:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-europe-s-gen-z-protesters-unite-over-living-costs-housing-and-uncertainty-of-getting-jobs--7a88fa7032d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-europe-s-gen-z-protesters-unite-over-living-costs-housing-and-uncertainty-of-getting-jobs" /><summary type="html">Although French high schoolers may have taken the lead in the youth protests that have since spread to Belgium, Germany, Italy, Portugal and Spain, they acted like "a catalyst" for their shared concerns over their future, researchers say, pointing to higher living costs, unaffordable housing and the uncertainty of their employment prospects.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes kill at least 26 in Ukraine after war's longest ceasefire ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd33b3947aca0a8d9e3ec5a751be89d38ee1db141115dbfa8793f408422ae0d3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T01:18:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-russian-strikes-kill-26-in-ukraine-after-longest-ceasefire-ends--a4e958250ed1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-russian-strikes-kill-26-in-ukraine-after-longest-ceasefire-ends" /><summary type="html">Russia killed at least 26 people in strikes on a village in southern Ukraine on Monday, including civilians collecting humanitarian aid, emergency workers and police officers. The attack came hours after a rare ceasefire ended, extinguishing hopes of progress towards peace.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Emergency alerts hacking 'designed to undermine trust in government', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b4f149611806ee7e8b0f00b639fe42c43e9a258a9e04949716102198dd6acfa</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T22:30:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261102-emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says--3e24a09abf48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261102-emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Emergency alert systems in Russia and Ukraine were hit in cyberattacks overnight, with fake warnings of possible nuclear strikes broadcast to users in both countries. The systems have since been brought back under control, though much remains unclear about the attacks, including who was responsible. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr Melanie Garson, Associate Professor in International Security at University College London. She says that these kinds of attacks "are designed to undermine faith in the government's ability to provide trust".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Emergency alerts hacking 'designed to undermine trust in government', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e6b4355a799635d9f46b5628bbfd52e6cd7609e848d804f4ae5676ad6c0cef9</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T22:28:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says--2d0c015e47b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Emergency alert systems in Russia and Ukraine were hit in cyberattacks overnight, with fake warnings of possible nuclear strikes broadcast to users in both countries. The systems have since been brought back under control, though much remains unclear about the attacks, including who was responsible. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr Melanie Garson, Associate Professor in International Security at University College London. She says that these kinds of attacks "are designed to undermine faith in the government's ability to provide trust".</summary></entry><entry><title>The Long Hull: Karl Bushby reflects on perseverance &amp; 'best of humanity' on his 28-year journey home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66df82e895e19e418cc3f8b8aab4e3616564e282545c6307ff75276d9b933d4a</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T20:54:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261102-the-long-hull-karl-bushby-reflects-on-perseverance-best-of-humanity-on-his-28-year-journey---36a7e13bd371.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261102-the-long-hull-karl-bushby-reflects-on-perseverance-best-of-humanity-on-his-28-year-journey-home" /><summary type="html">"They say it takes a village. In this case, it took a world." After 28 years and some 50,000 kilometres, British explorer and adventurer Karl Bushby has returned to his hometown of Hull, completing an extraordinary life journey across four continents that illustrates not only the limits of human endurance, but also the intricate relationship between individual determination, geopolitical constraints and a world of humanity.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>EU says fridge attacks 'deliberate attempt to disrupt' bloc's food supply</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce63375459672180ddc3686688b04d6e6c85766dea46fb962c73584015cc762e</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T20:30:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-says-fridge-attacks-deliberate-attempt-to-disrupt-bloc-s-food-supply--66c4d792c545.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-fridge-attacks-deliberate-attempt-to-disrupt-bloc-s-food-supply" /><summary type="html">Grocery stores from Sweden to Portugal were hit Monday by a suspected cyberattack on their freezer systems, in what the EU denounced as a deliberate attempt to disrupt the bloc's food chain. Supermarkets in Belgium, Estonia, Finland, Ireland, Luxembourg and the Netherlands were among at least eight countries affected in the incident, which came three weeks after a cyberattack caused mass disruption in French grocery stores. Food retailers were forced to throw out produce that had spoiled or was at risk of spoiling after refrigerator temperatures soared overnight. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia again pummels Ukraine after rare pause in fighting in Kherson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc46a3a7da34a245e4895b7572b27724014af23936b969ebb7f4536a48dc1b4a</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T18:53:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-russia-pummels-ukraine-again-after-rare-pause-in-fighting-in-kherson--2e4e1b64c914.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-russia-pummels-ukraine-again-after-rare-pause-in-fighting-in-kherson" /><summary type="html">Intense fighting between Russia and Ukraine again picked up after a rare ceasefire allowed for a humanitarian mission to reach the war-torn, Russian-occupied city of Oleshky in the southern Kherson region. While Russia accused Kyiv of sending hundreds of drones toward Moscow overnight into Tuesday, Kyiv said Russia had killed dozens of civilians lining up for aid in Zaporizhzhia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Refrigeration cyberattacks highlight risks of connecting industry to the internet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cde8f68eb9fd4ba045069302719fdc1aceade3911f09345a0b56059c8ec88a7e</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T17:29:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-caught-cold-fridge-cyberattack-highlights-internet-gadget-weaknesses--721c22a98b74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-caught-cold-fridge-cyberattack-highlights-internet-gadget-weaknesses" /><summary type="html">Cyberattacks affecting supermarket refrigeration systems on Monday in several European countries – including Belgium, Estonia, Finland, Ireland, Luxembourg, the Netherlands and Sweden – have highlighted the risks of connecting industrial infrastructure to the internet.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>British adventurer arrives back at mother's home after 28-year journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:980f0c5fcc205f04ea21113f00b201347efd90f21f6b0dae48bc8b7d9e1f068c</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:45:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-british-adventurer-arrives-back-at-mother-s-home-after-28-year-journey--f46b5480775f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-british-adventurer-arrives-back-at-mother-s-home-after-28-year-journey" /><summary type="html">British adventurer Karl Bushby enjoyed an emotional reunion with his mother and family on Monday, as he arrived back home after a 28-year, 50,000-kilometre trek from South America, crossing four continents on foot.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia report fake emergency alerts after cyberattacks target apps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12377ae182adb14f3b73aabcd67e5142804963230adec08ef5c8f53de3fbd616</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:06:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-report-fake-emergency-alerts-after-cyberattacks-target-apps--d0b256d1a838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-report-fake-emergency-alerts-after-cyberattacks-target-apps" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Ukraine and Russia said their emergency alert mobile apps had been targeted by cyberattacks, with users in Ukraine receiving false warnings of an imminent nuclear threat. Moscow said that hackers had sent fake emergency alerts after gaining access to the Russian Emergency Situations Ministry’s mobile app, and that efforts were ongoing to restore the app's functionality.</summary></entry><entry><title>Fresh wave of fridge cyberattacks hits European supermarkets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eb2e88b5be5085ffe7a9b80198b0050319e270c4c5799926305e89b03208643</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:40:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-fresh-wave-of-fridge-cyberattacks-hits-european-supermarkets--81a7e18ccf01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-fresh-wave-of-fridge-cyberattacks-hits-european-supermarkets" /><summary type="html">Stores and supermarkets across Belgium, Luxembourg, Finland, Estonia and Sweden all reported early Monday abrupt temperature spikes in their fridges and freezers in an apparent cyberattack targeting refrigeration units. The incidents follow a similar attack that hit hundreds of supermarkets across France in October, triggering food loss and fires.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italian journalists under police protection as threats rise across the country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3f3e403e8a71ffd4af4f8ae2e08c691223e231e32a0ab0e059df7a355a12ab3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T13:20:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-italian-journalists-under-police-protection-as-threats-rise-across-the-country--830ee8076ae2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-italian-journalists-under-police-protection-as-threats-rise-across-the-country" /><summary type="html">Italy is the European country with the largest number of journalists under police protection. There, journalism is a profession particularly susceptible to threats and intimidation, but the European Union's measures to protect press freedom are slow to be implemented. FRANCE 24's team has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Consolidation of power': Bulgaria elects Iliana Iotova as first woman president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:210be5e2166398b93bbb289eb6bb3f36a15244985ee53120e7d5acdaba7b0240</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261102-consolidation-of-power-bulgaria-elects-iliana-iotova-as-first-woman-president--8be991b44926.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261102-consolidation-of-power-bulgaria-elects-iliana-iotova-as-first-woman-president" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, November 2: Bulgarian papers discuss the country's new president. In Belarus, some political prisoners are held in psychiatric wards instead of prisons. Also: Hitler's Eagle's Nest burned down. Will it be rebuilt and should it? Finally, the queen of Halloween, Heidi Klum, flaunts her most disgusting costume yet.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Former UK paratrooper Karl Bushby ends 28-year trek across jungles and frozen sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:621d8d214b7db18c10b0ca4473cda0bae99584185524aa3d227a7d1511ea3bf5</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T10:13:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-former-uk-paratrooper-karl-bushby-ends-28-year-trek-across-jungles-and-frozen-sea--6b241b23dc52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-former-uk-paratrooper-karl-bushby-ends-28-year-trek-across-jungles-and-frozen-sea" /><summary type="html">Former British paratrooper Karl Bushby on Monday came to the end of his 28-year trek around the world, arriving in his native city of Hull after having swum across the English Channel. His journey took him from the southern tip of Latin America up across the frozen Bering Strait before crossing through Central Asia and Europe to return home.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France: Some schools blocked as limited youth protests resume after holidays</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a38f6e6c40d6356e25f2ba812d3c9f4fa1d01f7e762f87035cf788c40b9a5d8</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T09:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-france-some-schools-blocked-as-limited-youth-protests-resume-after-holidays--e8fe347b0113.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-france-some-schools-blocked-as-limited-youth-protests-resume-after-holidays" /><summary type="html">French students returning from autumn holidays blocked some high schools on Monday, November 2, determined to reinvigorate a protest movement despite government concessions during the break. FRANCE 24's Antonia Kerrigan reports from the ground.</summary></entry></feed>
